---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '@esa/docs/base';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';

// Tier 2 — the layer to read, and the layer a theme re-points.
const scale = [
  { token: '--radius-xs', value: '0.125rem · 2px', role: 'Swatches, colour chips, inline markers' },
  { token: '--radius-sm', value: '0.25rem · 4px', role: 'Inputs and buttons at xs/sm; badges, tooltips, kbd' },
  { token: '--radius-md', value: '0.5rem · 8px', role: 'The default — fields at md/lg, menus, popovers, panels, cards' },
  { token: '--radius-lg', value: '0.75rem · 12px', role: 'Dialogs, command palette, entity search' },
  { token: '--radius-pill', value: '9999px', role: 'Avatars, progress bars, filter pills' },
];

// Tier 1 — the ingredients. Listed for orientation; never read one directly.
const primitives = [
  { token: '--radius-050', value: '0.125rem · 2px' },
  { token: '--radius-100', value: '0.25rem · 4px' },
  { token: '--radius-200', value: '0.5rem · 8px' },
  { token: '--radius-300', value: '0.5rem · 8px' },
  { token: '--radius-400', value: '0.75rem · 12px' },
  { token: '--radius-500', value: '1rem · 16px' },
  { token: '--radius-full', value: '9999px' },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Radius — Ecology" activeHref="/foundations/radius">
  <nav class="crumbs"><a href={withBase('/')}>Ecology</a> <span>/</span> <span>Foundations</span> <span>/</span> <span>Radius</span></nav>
  <h1>Radius</h1>
  <p class="lede">Corner rounding, from a barely-there hairline to fully circular. Pick by element scale — inputs and buttons round tightly, panels and dialogs round softly.</p>

  <Section id="scale" title="The scale">
    <p>
      These are the names to write. Each swatch renders with its actual token on all four corners.
      Radius is the one category where tier 2 is a <em>scale</em> rather than a set of intents —
      a corner can be derived from its position on a ramp, where a colour cannot. It carried roles
      (<code>--radius-surface</code>, <code>--radius-card</code>) until 2026-08-16; those still
      resolve as deprecated aliases, and <code>/update-tokens</code> rewrites them.
    </p>
    <div class="grid">
      {scale.map((s) => (
        <div class="cell">
          <div class="cell__swatch" style={`border-radius: var(${s.token})`}></div>
          <div class="cell__meta">
            <code>{s.token}</code>
            <span class="cell__value">{s.value}</span>
            <span class="cell__role">{s.role}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="usage" title="Usage">
    <p>Match radius to element size — mixing radii across nested elements (a sharp input inside a soft card) reads as intentional layering.</p>
    <pre class="snippet"><code>{`.button { border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem); }
.card   { border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 0.75rem); }
.avatar { border-radius: var(--radius-pill, 9999px); }`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      A theme re-points these, and <code>--radius-md</code> is the one to move first — it is the
      default corner and the most-used step, so it takes the whole kit flatter or rounder in a line.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="primitives" title="Ingredients (tier 1)">
    <p>
      The raw ramp the scale above is assembled from. Listed so the mapping is legible —
      <strong>never read one of these in a component and never re-point one in a theme.</strong>
      Moving a primitive moves everything downstream of it, which is the blast radius the tier
      model exists to prevent.
    </p>
    <ul class="prims">
      {primitives.map((p) => (
        <li><code>{p.token}</code><span>{p.value}</span></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="foot">
      <code>--radius-200</code> and <code>--radius-300</code> are the same value — a duplicate rung
      left over from when tier 2 pointed a separate role at each. Nothing references
      <code>--radius-300</code> now.
    </p>
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(160px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-400, 1rem); }
  .cell { border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: 10px; padding: var(--spacing-400, 1rem); }
  .cell__swatch { width: 100%; height: 88px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-background-brand, #43608a) 14%, var(--color-background-elevation-raised, #fff)); border: 1.5px solid var(--color-background-brand, #43608a); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem); }
  .cell__meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
  .cell__meta code { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default, #171717); }
  .cell__value { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #525252); }
  .cell__role { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default-muted, #737373); }

  .prims { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(210px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem); }
  .prims li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem); padding: var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem) var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 0.25rem); }
  .prims code { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default, #171717); }
  .prims span { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default-muted, #737373); }
  .foot { color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #525252); }

  .snippet { background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken, #f5f5f5); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: 10px; padding: var(--spacing-400, 1rem) var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem); overflow-x: auto; }
  .snippet code { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-content-default, #171717); }
</style>
